NICE-TO-HAVE FEATURES
===========================================================================
- could hunter exhil be detected by the idea that they only have one
  self-cast heal that requires a button press (i.e., isn't a proc) and also
  applies a hot? how to distinguish from health pot?
    - buttonPress
    - UNIT_COMBAT heal where the caster=target=a hunter
    - UNIT_AURA applied a HoT (basically required talent)
    - is SPELL_UPDATE_COOLDOWN sent to party? or only fires in the player's client
- more work to distinguish divine protection from wings
    - maybe this can work by adding inference on update? some of the wings versions
      fire update events and the ability can then be identified
    - however, for that to make DP show up as a center defensive the update inference
      logic would be that updates _MUST_ occur for the spell. how would DP know that
      it didn't receive an update and therefore should fire?
- [maybe] add CCs/stops if the blizzard CC flags cause uniquely identifiable events
- consolidate specialization/class/player info into a GetSlotInfo() function and
  stop delegating data management to the icon rows.  logic is all duplicated due
  to the tray+cd bars.
- visual on solver for abilities that can't be solved under ideal zero knowledge
  conditions (e.g., arcane mage surge and mirror images have identical flags
  and durations).
    - highlight these icons red
* ability database completeness is questionable
    - is looping through all spell IDs and dumping any with BIG, IMPORTANT or
      EXTERNAL flags exhaustive?
    - i only looked at all C_Spell.IsSpellHelpful()=true spells that were either
      BIG|IMP|EXT. there is a not_helpful_spells dump that needs a pass.  e.g.,
      fiery brand is only in the not_helpful list since it's a debuff.
- associate player ID token with rows so that on GROUP_ROSTER_UPDATEs we can
  potentially preserve data. very low priority - just clearing and resetting
  all data should be fine for real world use.
    - currently using player name from libspec
- add logic layer to detect when all possible CDs have been cast
    - how useful is this? suppose at time X we know every ability is on
      cooldown. then when the next ability is used, can assume the best case
      scenario for every ability (min CD across all abilities).  this could
      eliminate some possibilities.  e.g., DK uses AMS at time=1 and IBF at
      time=10.  so at time=10 both are on CD.  the min CD across the two is
      40s, so until time=10+IBF's cooldown, anymore abilities from that player
      must have been AMS.
- confidence layer -> confidence network
    - the abstract idea for confidence should be that of a network. each confidence
      method should state its level of confidence and the decided ability, then the
      network should check itself for consistency.
- look into required debuffs - the current code does not actually find debuffs,
  it finds things not flagged as HELPFUL. vampiric blood is an example of where
  this doesn't behave as expected
    - could be why bop and spellwarding didn't detect forbearance? even though it
      worked for bubble..
    - [UPDATE] bop/spellwarding: the forbearance aura comes in a different UNIT_AURA
      even. could it be caused casting on other units vs self? YEP, when cast on self
      BoP and forbearance arrive in the same UNIT_AURA
- confidence network: handle death
    - on death all auras are removed with a UNIT_AURA call, but all duration rules
      need to be treated as DURATION_LTE.
- inferAbility() - save the conflicting spells/casters for UI elements
- would be nice to firm up two object classes: Buff and HistoryItem, where Buff represents
  the aura itself and HistoryItem only handles tracking and display duties.
- updating/clearing tracker data
    - when party members join/leave group or change positions
    - could be easier to just clear for now, but could be annoying if,
      e.g., you're looking at CDs when a key ends and a group member drops
      party and deletes all of your info.
    - update (likely clear, since there is a memory leak by design) between keys.
	    - is there a different event when changing zones vs. starting a mythic+ key?
    - add reset button to the /pdh solution window
- get data to make better estimates on duration solve tolerance
    - both the "match" epsilon and the minimum difference
- how to handle sac in "solved" interface? (since its duration is _less than or
    equal to_ 12s, meaning it clashes with almost every defensive buff
    - solved interface should perhaps be the most conservative solution, meaning
      exact duration matches, no advanced inference (CD tracking, variable duration, etc)
    - turns out there's an external flag on sac, so this is less of a problem
    - need to figure out ironbark+sac in the same group
- consider aurasUpdated logic layer
    - turns out almost everything about fiery brand is bugged so can't work on this
    - can be useful for fiery brand, sentinel (due to buff stacks ticking down)
- better handle CDR
    - can compute upper bounds (or averages) on the amount of CDR gained. e.g., throwing
      avenger's shield on CD at 5 targets = 5s CDR per 12s (though procs reduce this
      and so does divine toll).:
- consider a different event than OnUpdate for cooldown timers since this
  fires every frame.



